			"date": "2025-03-24T13:59:10.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Diving into it now. It seems that socket.dev sources its info from osv.dev, which claims the package has embedded malicious code. Not sure where that is coming from.<br>- <a href=\"https://test.osv.dev/vulnerability/MAL-2022-3326\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">test.osv.dev/vulnerability/MAL</span><span class=\"invisible\">-2022-3326</span></a><br>- <a href=\"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/506.html\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions</span><span class=\"invisible\">/506.html</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
